{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base","id":290230,"title":"3E: Solar Secret Societies - Being sneaky while building a power base.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-22T20:06:23-07:00","id":290230,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> 3E: Solar Secret Societies - Being sneaky while building a power base.","content":"There are a few ways to play a Solar. By their nature they tend to stand out, but even a Dawn when motivated can downplay what they are, act covertly and still be heroically awesome when doing it. So let's say I want to play an Agent's of UCS game. My Solars are going to be sneaky when they can, and fade fast when they can't. And lets also say I have a number of players down with that style of game.<br /> <br /> Where would I start?<br /> <br /> Obvious tricks would be using Socialize Charms to send covert messages. Mix in some Bureaucracy and social influence with the right people to make people turn a blind eye. Call it the Batman effect. Gordon must know Bruce Wayne is Batman by now, but doesn't care. The good he does out ways the vigilante he should bring it. In the case of the Solars they have respectable 'Day Jobs' in the local community and when the threat of Realm bullying, Deathlord meddling, etc happens they quietly pull out the Daiklaves and clean up the mess. Then go back to smiling at the major as if nothing happened.<br /> <br /> Zeniths and Eclipse would dominate this style play.<br /> <br /> I could see Dawn's by virtue of firepower and Nights by virtue of stealth being next in the 'fast but quiet' tier of tricks.<br /> <br /> The only cast, or player style that might run afowl of this is the Twilight or Sorcerer characters. Just way too much raw magic being thrown around. <br /> <br /> How would you resolve that? What sorts of adaptations would you make in possible 3E builds to be sneaky while effective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T21:35:10-07:00","id":290289,"title":"","content":"Twilights have more than just Sorcery. They are Investigative powerhouses, can deal directly with Spirits and then there is Craft. &quot;Where does he get those wonderful toys&quot; indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1840-akashicmonk","name":"akashicmonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T21:43:40-07:00","id":290291,"title":"","content":"My default play style in a lot of the games I was in was to appear as human as possible until I got around Essence 3-4 and had two or three dozen charms under my belt, so I'll post some things I learned / strategies I developed.<br /> <br /> Only use your personal motepool. Your peripheral motepool? You don't have one. It only appears if you're about to die. Your charms are super efficient compared to the other Exalts, use that to your benefit.<br /> <br /> For combat, get charms that have a scene long duration and use them like your life depended on it. Shining Razor Wind, Iron Kettle Body and Flows like Blood can all help you not die while still keeping you at superhuman level without it being overtly supernatural.<br /> <br /> Lion's Roar Recovery is your best friend. Increase your stunt value by one step? Yes please!<br /> <br /> Sagacious Reading of Intent + 2nd Presence Excellency will make you very capable in the social arena until you can afford to branch out a bit more.<br /> <br /> Beyond this, many charms don't have the obvious keyword, so careful resource management can help you a lot when you need to use non-combat, non-social skills.<br /> <br /> Stealth has a charm that lets your Night share their stealth effects with their team. Spreading the Night's Shroud, I believe.<br /> <br /> If you can get away with it, try stunting any Obvious flickers of Anima as being Fire Aspect instead of Solar. This won't help when your Caste Mark starts to shine, but will help you with any Obvious Charms.<br /> <br /> Human teammates can be an excellent force multiplier at lower essence levels. Work with them to avoid using more essence than you absolutely have to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T21:43:41-07:00","id":290292,"title":"","content":"A twilight in an espionage type game would actually be quite beneficial because they will be the groups &quot;Q&quot;. they can craft the items the agents use and also use magic ahead of time to insure their group has the advantage in any encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T22:11:39-07:00","id":290313,"title":"","content":"Generally? Play to your strengths, do something that seems plausible to explain away your abilities, or act in a way that puts you way outside of suspicion.<br /> <br /> In the past I have had an Eclipse in a 3e playtest that simply avoided ever showing his anima and had strong coloration indicating he was a wood aspect (born into a major house of the isle) and that was pretty much it. He kept it subtle and wasn't especially good at combat.<br /> <br /> Let's see, I had another character that when pressed referred to himself as &quot;A Prince of the Earth very strongly aspected to Water&quot; Which was technically true as he was a Defiler chosen of Kimbery. He stuck mostly to martial arts especially the water themed ones and easily managed to pass himself off as a very strong DB when it mattered.<br /> <br /> I've also gone the exact reverse of subtle and stole a classical idea... He was a Zenith rich retired from the guild man turned &quot;Anathema Hunter&quot;. He would periodically lead &quot;Wyld Purges&quot; into the countryside, and when not doing that would charge around Nexus attacking/accusing people of being Anathema. After which of course his servants would wander by, apologize for the crazy old man being a crazy old man and pay for the damages. Even gave him a shaving basin for a hat, 'cause you might as well go whole-hog when you rip something off.<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing to remember is that what you have to hide is very much dependent on the audience. The OP sorcery example, you don't need to hide the power/level of your sorcery, except from other sorcerers. The tales about such people are wild and fanciful and terrifying, so your typical army grunt isn't going to have any idea that you're not supposed to be able to throw around forces like that, with that level of ease... that's exactly the kind of thing that he's heard of sorcerers doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T00:47:06-07:00","id":290343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>akashicmonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base?p=290289#post290289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilights have more than just Sorcery. They are Investigative powerhouses, can deal directly with Spirits and then there is Craft. &quot;Where does he get those wonderful toys&quot; indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to four and a half Twilight Abilities that have nothing to do with Sorcery, not every spell is as showy as Flight of the Brilliant Raptor. Have the Night plant a Coin of Distant Vision to listen in on people. Silence an inconvenient witness with Corrupted Words or Theft of Memory. Hide with Disguise of the New Face. Use Droning Suggestion or Peacock Shadow Eyes to supplement your social rolls. Cast Shadow Summons, Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares or The Spy Who Walks in Darkness in the safety of your home. Ambush someone with Mists of Eventide (or lure in a random pigeon with Commanding the Beasts for a subtle spy) followed by Sorcerer's Irresistible Puppetry.<br /> <br /> And when shit hits the fan, throw a Brilliant Raptor and escape in the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T01:33:08-07:00","id":290351,"title":"","content":"Regarding Sorcery: While it is almost certain that you are going to be glowing by the end of any major use, most non-combat instances of sorcery do not suffer from being performed far away in a secure location. Demons or elementals can turn immaterial and sneak around with you or on errands, travel spells can be stopped short of your destination, and no one has to see you cast Whirlwind of Fate for you to gain the bonus from it.<br /> <br /> Edit: There is also an archery charm I believe that lets you shot your anima into other things or people. The &quot;sacred tree&quot; that glows with the holy light of the Sun might be a sign of divine favor rather than the mark of an ancient demon.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Yes, Flashing Sunspot Attack. It also lets you use your Archery charms without flaring your own anima. Be careful though, someone might still be suspicious when you shoot the enemy general from ten miles away through a tornado.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 10-23-2014, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T01:39:03-07:00","id":290369,"title":"","content":"This seems less about actual secret societies and more about just being a set of covert individuals...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T08:38:04-07:00","id":290521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base?p=290369#post290369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems less about actual secret societies and more about just being a set of covert individuals...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to get to that but good point. The core idea is setting up a secret society as your support next work. Once you work out the logistics of being sneaky.<br /> <br /> I was hinting at recruiting the local leaders into your ruse. Sending coded messages hidden in popular written plays, bar songs, etc. Then using yiur charmsto build resource and ccommunication networks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T09:13:23-07:00","id":290542,"title":"","content":"I feel as though the main thing one would need is some cause or recruitment mechanism that necessarily draws the socially disaffected, if not outlawed altogether, who might be driven towards coordinated or mutually supportive activities either in service of a subversive goal, or generally aiding one another in a manner that is desired to not be subject to scrutiny by society at large.<br /> <br /> Actually being sneaky isn't necessarily difficult, just a matter of making sure you know a decently out of the way place to which people can arrive in a staggered manner (or just find or build places with secret tunnels, and make sure the proper people are bribed and records destroyed), and then select an arbitrary form of code words and hand signs.<br /> <br /> If one wishes to play an Exalt who is managing the thing in a fairly decentralized but meticulously managed system, I'd say Larceny and similar Charms are very good for passing yourself off as several different figures who are all ostensibly part of a network of intermediaries between the cells and the mysterious leader. Or Bureaucracy to <i>actually</i> have such a network. The key image, I think, is that everybody perceives things in terms of reporting to somebody who reports to somebody who reports to the leader, and only ever knowing the step immediately above and below you, and it's never actually possible to trace it to the top because if you're not in disguise as a courier, then you're just intercepting the reports as they pass between people who never actually know how far they are from the top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T18:14:08-07:00","id":290924,"title":"","content":"Isator, what about setting up an informal communication network? You may not have it be more complicated than regional meet up with Solars and friendly 3rd parties, but do you think in a Solar centric game that networking as a Solar for potential collaborations would be good. The 'society' would be covert by need, but it would be nice to have mercenaries, safe houses, and supplies on tap for missions and causes you support. Solars have plenty of great communication (especially covert) in their trees that would befuddle all but the most dedicated Sidereal/Lunar looking for clues.<br /> <br /> I'm curious what sort of Solar societies might form: Anti-Realm, mutual protection, anti Deathlord, Sorcery/Crafting circles, Wyld Exploration, past life old &quot;friends&quot;, Nexus Trade Control, etc.<br /> <br /> It might make for a fun starting point for a game when the 'society' contacts you to join and aid them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T19:29:46-07:00","id":296389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mostlyjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base#post290230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only cast, or player style that might run afowl of this is the Twilight or Sorcerer characters. Just way too much raw magic being thrown around.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Twilight can be a master detective to rival Sherlock Holmes or Batman, legendary physicians on par with Aesculapius or Master Li, master craftsman who can forge divine wonders when they must, or world-changing savants like Aristotle or Confucius. Even if you're Occult-focused, being an exorcist or shaman isn't necessarily something that would make you always &quot;stand out.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's also the new Caste Abilities they get in the flexible system, but I'm not sure if those have been spoiled with. What I will say is that they definitely facilitate Twilights running covert societies, spy networks, mystery cults, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T19:35:45-07:00","id":296393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base?p=296389#post296389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the new Caste Abilities they get in the flexible system, but I'm not sure if those have been spoiled with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, yes, yes, they have. But you should list them again for clarity's sake.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*sigh* No, they haven't.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T19:41:10-07:00","id":296394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base?p=296393#post296393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why, yes, yes, they have. But you should list them again for clarity's sake.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*sigh* No, they haven't.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to hazard a guess at bureaucracy, linguistics if it's seven and maybe integrity or possibly awareness if it's eight. Bureaucracy and linguistics are pretty obvious and either awareness to augment investigation or integrity to augment the fact that they stare into the abyss and it stares back into them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T19:54:53-07:00","id":296419,"title":"","content":"Also there's always a terrible bittersweet feeling when a dev says something will work so much better in 3E. One the one hand it's like &quot;YES! Sweet! I wanted that to work so much better every time I tried to do it!&quot; and on the other it's like &quot;Well we don't have even the barest bit of that yet so shut up.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T08:31:05-07:00","id":297138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base?p=296394#post296394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to hazard a guess at bureaucracy, linguistics if it's seven and maybe integrity or possibly awareness if it's eight. Bureaucracy and linguistics are pretty obvious and either awareness to augment investigation or integrity to augment the fact that they stare into the abyss and it stares back into them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Ex3 Linguistics is no longer tied to how many languages you speak, what part of the Ability used for writing soul-stirring poetry ties into the caste of genius intellectuals?<br /> <br /> I mean, 2e's Linguistics directly imparted a language with each dot, so you might end up favoring it if you want to play one of those improbable characters from <i>Criminal Minds</i> (&quot;My reading speed is high enough for me to read <i>Atlas Shrugged</i> during my lunch break. Four times.&quot;), but we've been directly told that won't be the case for Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T09:54:40-07:00","id":297196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base?p=297138#post297138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Ex3 Linguistics is no longer tied to how many languages you speak, what part of the Ability used for writing soul-stirring poetry ties into the caste of genius intellectuals?<br /> <br /> I mean, 2e's Linguistics directly imparted a language with each dot, so you might end up favoring it if you want to play one of those improbable characters from <i>Criminal Minds</i> (&amp;quot;My reading speed is high enough for me to read <i>Atlas Shrugged</i> during my lunch break. Four times.&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, but we've been directly told that won't be the case for Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://criticalcarelondon.ca/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Koninck_Salomon-ZZZ-An_Old_Scholar.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://criticalcarelondon.ca/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Koninck_Salomon-ZZZ-An_Old_Scholar.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://criticalcarelondon.ca/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Koninck_Salomon-ZZZ-An_Old_Scholar.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://criticalcarelondon.ca/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Koninck_Salomon-ZZZ-An_Old_Scholar.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> First search result on google images for &quot;scholar&quot;. Since the dawn of enlightenment writing and knowledge have been pretty inseparable. It's what allowed such great exchanges of ideas and methods as well as allowing many of those that followed to stand on the shoulders of the giants who came before them. Linguistics may no longer mean extra languages, but it will always mean writing and reading, and likely be involved in decrypting ciphers and such. It has been in the past and there's been no mention otherwise.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly thematic to have an ancient solar loremaster leafing through ancient tomes and seeing through the complex code that the author used to hide his ideas in plain sight. Like in Dan Browns Angels and Demons, the hidden path of illumination hidden in books where only the enlightened would see them. That's some serious Twilight shit right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T23:58:08-07:00","id":297878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/290230-3e-solar-secret-societies-being-sneaky-while-building-a-power-base?p=296419#post296419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there's always a terrible bittersweet feeling when a dev says something will work so much better in 3E. One the one hand it's like &quot;YES! Sweet! I wanted that to work so much better every time I tried to do it!&quot; and on the other it's like &quot;Well we don't have even the barest bit of that yet so shut up.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E or 2E you could to the things I'm suggesting. It's just I'm hoping the new social influence rules help making some of the management in 3E easier. That's all I care about. And thank goodness for the death of social 2E combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}